#! @Chapter Enumeration of saturated fusion systems
#! @ChapterLabel EnumerationSaturated

#! The operation <Ref Oper="AllSaturatedFusionSystems" Label="for IsPGroup"/> constructs all saturated fusion systems on a $p$-group $S$ up to
#! isomorphism, including those with $O_p(\mathcal{F}) \neq 1$ or $O^p(\mathcal{F}) \neq \mathcal{F}$. It follows
#! <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Section 4"/>. All tests used to discard subgroups, automizers or fusion data before the saturation test
#! hold for every saturated fusion system (not only for reduced ones). Tests which depend on the classification of finite simple groups
#! are marked as such in Section <Ref Sect="Section_PotentiallyEssential"/>.

#! @Section The algorithm

#! * The $S$-conjugacy classes of $S$-centric subgroups are split into $\textrm{Aut}(S)$-orbits. For one subgroup $E$ in each orbit, the tests of
#!   Section <Ref Sect="Section_PotentiallyEssential"/> are applied, and the list of all subgroups $Y \leq \textrm{Out}(E)$ with Sylow $p$-subgroup
#!   $\textrm{Out}_S(E)$, $O_p(Y) = 1$ and a strongly $p$-embedded subgroup is computed with
#!   <Ref Oper="OvergroupsWithSylowSubgroup" Label="for IsGroup, IsGroup"/>. This is done once, independently of $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$.
#! * $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S) = \textrm{Inn}(S) C$, where $C$ runs through the $p'$-subgroups of $\textrm{Out}(S)$ up to conjugacy.
#! * For each choice of $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$, the candidates for essential subgroups are representatives $E$ of the
#!   $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$-orbits in the $\textrm{Aut}(S)$-orbits above, with $|N_S(E)|$ maximal. The candidates for $\textrm{Out}_\mathcal{F}(E)$
#!   are the subgroups $Y$ above (transported to $E$ by an automorphism of $S$) which contain the restrictions of the stabilizer of $E$ in
#!   $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$.
#! * The fusion data are the subsets of the candidate essential subgroups with a choice of automizers. They are enumerated by a depth first
#!   search through the candidates ordered by decreasing size, which discards a partial choice as soon as it violates
#!   <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Proposition 4.10(1)"/>: if $n$ is the largest order of a chosen essential subgroup and $E$ is chosen with
#!   $|N_S(E)| > n$, or $|N_S(E)| = n$ and $N_S(E)$ is not $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$-conjugate to a chosen subgroup, then
#!   $N_{\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(E)}(\textrm{Aut}_S(E))$ consists of restrictions of elements of $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$.
#! * Each remaining fusion datum is tested with <Ref Prop="IsSaturatedFusionSystem" Label="for IsFusionSystem"/>, and isomorphic copies are removed
#!   with the method of <Ref Oper="IsomorphismFusionSystems" Label="for IsFusionSystem, IsFusionSystem"/>.
#!
#! By default, no restriction on $O_p(\mathcal{F})$ or $O^p(\mathcal{F})$ is made. Two options restrict the output:
#! * `CoreFree`: only fusion systems with $O_p(\mathcal{F}) = 1$ are returned. If $S \neq 1$ is abelian, there are none
#!   <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Lemma 4.1"/>. A choice of $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$ is skipped, and a fusion datum is discarded before the saturation
#!   test, if a nontrivial subgroup of the intersection of the (chosen) candidate essential subgroups is invariant under $\textrm{Inn}(S)$,
#!   $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$ and all (chosen) candidate automizers <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Lemma 4.9"/>.
#! * `FullFocal`: only fusion systems with $O^p(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{F}$ are returned. By <Cite Key="AKO" Where="Corollary I.7.5"/> (see also
#!   <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Lemma 2.6(2)"/>), this holds if and only if $\textrm{foc}(\mathcal{F}) = \textrm{hyp}(\mathcal{F}) = S$, and
#!   $\textrm{foc}(\mathcal{F}) = S$ suffices. For the fusion system $\mathcal{F}$ generated by $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$ and automizers $A_i$ of
#!   subgroups $E_i$, $\textrm{foc}(\mathcal{F})$ is generated by $[S, S]$ and the elements $x^{-1} \alpha(x)$ where $x$ and $\alpha$ run through
#!   generators of $E_i$ and $A_i$ (or of $S$ and $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$). By Burnside's basis theorem, $\textrm{foc}(\mathcal{F}) = S$ if and only if
#!   the images of these elements span $S/\Phi(S)$. This is a linear algebra condition which is tested during the depth first search,
#!   before any saturation test, and for each choice of $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$ with all candidates together. Moreover, for $p \geq 5$
#!   the choice $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S) = \textrm{Inn}(S)$ is skipped <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Lemma 4.2"/>, <Cite Key="DGMP" Where="Corollary 6.2"/>.
#!
#! Both options can be combined: `AllSaturatedFusionSystems(S : CoreFree, FullFocal)`.

#! @Section Potentially essential subgroups
#! @SectionLabel PotentiallyEssential

#! A subgroup $E$ of $S$ is discarded as a candidate for an essential subgroup if one of the following conditions fails. For each of them,
#! the source is given; all of them hold for every saturated fusion system on $S$.
#! * $E$ is a proper, $S$-centric and non-cyclic subgroup of $S$ <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Proposition 4.8(1),(2)"/>.
#! * If $g \in N_S(E)$ acts trivially on $E/\Theta\Phi(E)$ and on $\Theta\Phi(E)/\Phi(E)$ for $\Theta = 1, Z(E)$ or $Z_2(E)$, then $g \in E$
#!   <Cite Key="OV" Where="Lemma 3.4"/>. For $\Theta = 1$, this is <Ref Oper="FrattiniTest" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/>.
#! * $N = \textrm{Out}_S(E)$ is isomorphic to a Sylow $p$-subgroup of a group with a strongly $p$-embedded subgroup which acts faithfully on
#!   $E/\Phi(E)$. Hence $|N|^2 \leq |E/\Phi(E)|$ and $N$ has one of the types of <Cite Key="SAM14" Where="Theorem 6.9"/> (see also
#!   <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Corollary 4.6, Lemma 4.7, Proposition 4.8(3),(4)"/>). For $p = 2$, this rests on Bender's classification of groups
#!   with a strongly embedded subgroup and Higman's classification of Suzuki $2$-groups;
#!   **for odd $p$, it depends on the classification of finite simple groups**. This test replaces <Ref Oper="RankTest" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/>.
#! * $\textrm{Aut}_S(E) \cap O_p(\textrm{Aut}(E)) = \textrm{Inn}(E)$ <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Proposition 4.8(2)"/>. This is
#!   <Ref Oper="RadicalTest" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/>.
#! * If $\textrm{Out}_S(E)$ contains an elementary abelian subgroup of order $p^2$, then $\textrm{Out}(E)$ and the candidates for
#!   $\textrm{Out}_\mathcal{F}(E)$ are not soluble <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Lemma 4.4, Proposition 4.8(5)"/>.
#! * For $p = 2$, the conditions of <Cite Key="AOV17" Where="Proposition 2.3(a),(c)-(f),(j)"/>, which rest on Bender's theorem:
#!   <Ref Oper="Zed0Test" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/> <Cite Key="OV" Where="Lemma 3.6(a)"/>, the structure of $\textrm{Out}_S(E)$
#!   <Cite Key="OV" Where="Proposition 3.3(a)"/>, the transitivity of $N_{\textrm{Out}(E)}(\textrm{Out}_S(E))$ on the involutions of $\textrm{Out}_S(E)$
#!   <Cite Key="OV" Where="Proposition 3.3(b)"/>, and lower bounds for the ranks of $E/\Phi(E)$ and of $[s, E/\Phi(E)]$ for
#!   $1 \neq s \in \textrm{Out}_S(E)$ <Cite Key="OV" Where="Lemma 1.7, Proposition 3.3(c),(d)"/>; this includes
#!   <Ref Oper="ModuleTest" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/>.
#!
#! For odd $p$, <Ref Oper="Zed0Test" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/> is not proved and therefore not used. The tests
#! <Ref Oper="LiftTest" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup, IsInt"/> and <Ref Oper="ValidAutTest" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup, IsInt"/> are not needed, since
#! the candidates for $\textrm{Out}_\mathcal{F}(E)$ are computed exactly. The automizers of <Ref Oper="ValidAutomizers" Label="for IsPGroup, IsPGroup"/>
#! are generated by $p$-elements, so they only cover fusion systems with $O^{p'}(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{F}$.

#! @Section Operations

#! @Description
#! Returns a list of all saturated fusion systems on the $p$-group $S$ up to isomorphism. With the option `CoreFree`
#! (for instance `AllSaturatedFusionSystems(S : CoreFree)`), only those with $O_p(\mathcal{F}) = 1$ are returned, and with the option `FullFocal`
#! only those with $O^p(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{F}$. With both options, the result consists of the saturated fusion systems with
#! $O_p(\mathcal{F}) = 1$ and $O^p(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{F}$, as in <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Section 5"/> (where also $O^{p'}(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{F}$ is required).
#! @Arguments S
#! @Returns a list of fusion systems
DeclareOperation("AllSaturatedFusionSystems", [IsPGroup]);

#! @BeginExampleSession
#! gap> S := SmallGroup(27, 3);;
#! gap> Length(AllSaturatedFusionSystems(S));
#! 15
#! gap> Length(AllSaturatedFusionSystems(S : CoreFree));
#! 4
#! gap> Length(AllSaturatedFusionSystems(S : FullFocal));
#! 12
#! gap> Length(AllSaturatedFusionSystems(S : CoreFree, FullFocal));
#! 4
#! @EndExampleSession

#! @Description
#! Let $T \neq 1$ be a $p$-subgroup of the finite group $G$. Returns representatives, up to conjugation in $N_G(T)$, of all subgroups $H \leq G$
#! containing $T$ such that $T$ is a Sylow $p$-subgroup of $H$. This follows <Cite Key="PS_MAGMA" Where="Appendix B"/>: the candidates for
#! $O^{p'}(H)$ are obtained by descending from the subnormal closure of $T$ in $G$ through maximal subgroups containing a conjugate of $T$,
#! and then $H = O^{p'}(H) N_H(T)$ by the Frattini argument. Only maximal subgroups and normal closures are computed, and not the
#! conjugacy classes of all subgroups of $G$.
#! @Arguments G T
#! @Returns a list of groups
DeclareOperation("OvergroupsWithSylowSubgroup", [IsGroup, IsGroup]);

#! @Description
#! Returns a list of all subgroups $X \leq \textrm{Aut}(E)$ which are candidates for $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(E)$ for an $\mathcal{F}$-essential subgroup $E$ of
#! $S$ in a saturated fusion system $\mathcal{F}$ with $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S) = \langle \textrm{Inn}(S), AS \rangle$: $E$ passes the tests of
#! Section <Ref Sect="Section_PotentiallyEssential"/>, $X/\textrm{Inn}(E)$ has the Sylow $p$-subgroup $\textrm{Out}_S(E)$, a trivial $p$-core and a strongly
#! $p$-embedded subgroup, and $X$ contains the restrictions of the stabilizer of $E$ in $\textrm{Aut}_\mathcal{F}(S)$. If $N_S(E) = S$, then
#! $N_X(\textrm{Aut}_S(E))$ consists of such restrictions.
#! @Arguments S, E, AS
#! @Returns a list of groups of automorphisms
DeclareOperation("EssentialAutomizerCandidates", [IsPGroup, IsPGroup, IsList]);
